    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏagmentum</span></b> , i, n.
		cogo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				joining together;</i> in concr., <i>a joint</i>
			(in good prose; not in Cic.; mostly in plur.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.,
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 42, 20 sq.</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 18, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Most. 3, 2, 143</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 3, 105 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2, 3, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 8, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 4,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a joining</i> or <i>connecting together</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syllabarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					17, 9, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
